 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542798,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "With the data in <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/Chapter8_Data-Sets\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\"NHL19,\"</a> use Google Sheets to create a scatter plot for points (PTS) vs. wins (W).",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBa3dHIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--c03501856c5f6daba10bea7127414162fdfbdb73/CS_Figure_08_08_109.jpg\" alt=\"A scatter plot represents PTS versus W. The horizontal axis representing W ranges from 25 to 65, in increments of 5. The vertical axis representing PTS ranges from 50 to 130, in increments of 20. The points are arranged in increasing order. Some of the points are as follows: (32, 70), (35, 80), (40, 88), (45, 100), and (50, 108). Note: all values are approximate.\">"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In Google Sheets, highlight the data including the headers.</p>\n<p>Open a copy of the file in Google Sheets. You cannot edit the original file.</p>\n<p>Look for the NHL19 tab.</p>\n<p>It will be easier for Google to suggest what you want if your columns are adjacent. Copy the Points column to the left of the Wins column.</p>\n<p>Highlight the columns for PTS (Points) and W (Wins), (including the headers).</p>\n<p>Choose Insert, then choose Chart.</p>\n<p>It may suggest a line chart in “Chart type.”</p>\n<p>In the Chart type drop down box, choose a scatter plot.</p>\n<p>Make sure that you see “W” on the horizontal axis.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
